{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK69mSPo2WWAgTgNC3Wf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug: both username validators now reject usernames that end with a newline. In `django/contrib/auth/validators.py`, `ASCIIUsernameValidator` and `UnicodeUsernameValidator` now use the pattern `r'\\A[\\w.@+-]+\\Z'` instead of `r'^[\\w.@+-]+$'`. The issue's point is that `$` also matches just before a trailing newline, while `\\Z` matches only at the very end of the string. I also swapped `^` for `\\A`, as the issue suggested, to keep the two ends consistent.\n\nThe existing `auth_tests.test_validators` suite passes (22 tests). I didn't add a test for the newline case, since the rules say not to edit test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":19218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":159},"output_tokens":241,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9daf7dc5-a14d-4d01-bd06-8995b016b472","uuid":"88fc51bd-a336-46f1-9cb6-f61533e4f935","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:42:39.080Z","request_id":"req_011ChK69mHCz1BWECNGBUjvo"}
